# Installed by "sudo ./bootstrap.sh slice" to /etc/udev/rules.d, beside the unit
# it names. Memory added to a running host: systemd works out a percentage
# MemoryMax only when it loads the unit, so tehas.slice keeps the size of the
# memory the host had when it booted until someone reloads systemd by hand. The
# rule asks systemd-udevd for that reload when a block comes online, so nobody
# has to. A oneshot unit does the reload rather than RUN+=: udevd kills a RUN
# that runs too long, and many blocks come online at once. Memory going offline
# needs nothing: the slice shrinks at the next reload.
SUBSYSTEM=="memory", ACTION=="online", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="tehas-slice-reload.service"
